      "rendered": "<div id=\"\" class=\"hds-media-detail-hero nasa-gb-align-wide width-full maxw-full margin-y-5 desktop:margin-y-7 padding-x-3 media-detail-hero--suppress-inner-media-caption hds-module alignwide wp-block-nasa-blocks-media-detail-hero\">\t<div class=\"grid-container grid-container-block padding-x-0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"label margin-bottom-1\">APOD</p>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"heading-22 margin-top-0 margin-bottom-2\">Astronomy Picture of the Day</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"p-md margin-top-0 margin-bottom-3 media-detail-hero__subtext\">\n\t\t\t\t<a href=\"/apod/archive/\">Discover the cosmos!</a> Each day a different image or photograph of our fascinating universe is featured, along with a brief explanation written by a professional astronomer.\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"media-detail-hero__media margin-bottom-6\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"wp-block-smd-block-image-rollover smd-image-rollover hds-module hds-media smd-image-rollover--clickable-indicators\"><div class=\"smd-image-rollover__alignment margin-left-auto margin-right-auto nasa-block-align-full\"><div class=\"smd-image-rollover__frame\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1255\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_2000.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=1255&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" class=\"smd-image-rollover__image smd-image-rollover__image--primary\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_2000.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=1255&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2000w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_2000.jpg?w=300&amp;h=188&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_2000.jpg?w=768&amp;h=482&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_2000.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=643&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1024w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_2000.jpg?w=1536&amp;h=964&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1536w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_2000.jpg?w=400&amp;h=251&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_2000.jpg?w=600&amp;h=377&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_2000.jpg?w=900&amp;h=565&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_2000.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=753&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1200w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2000px) 100vw, 2000px\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"2000\" height=\"1255\" src=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_2000.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=1255&amp;fit=clip&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\" class=\"smd-image-rollover__image smd-image-rollover__image--secondary\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_2000.jpg?w=2000&amp;h=1255&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 2000w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_2000.jpg?w=300&amp;h=188&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 300w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_2000.jpg?w=768&amp;h=482&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 768w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_2000.jpg?w=1024&amp;h=643&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1024w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_2000.jpg?w=1536&amp;h=964&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1536w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_2000.jpg?w=400&amp;h=251&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 400w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_2000.jpg?w=600&amp;h=377&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 600w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_2000.jpg?w=900&amp;h=565&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 900w, https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/2026/september/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_2000.jpg?w=1200&amp;h=753&amp;fit=crop&amp;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint 1200w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2000px) 100vw, 2000px\" /><div class=\"toggle-button-container padding-1\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"toggle-view-before-button margin-right-1px is-active\" aria-pressed=\"true\"><span class=\"toggle-view-before-label\">Original</span></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"toggle-view-after-button margin-left-1px\" aria-pressed=\"false\"><span class=\"toggle-view-after-label\">Annotated</span></button></div></div></div></div>\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h1 class=\"display-48 margin-top-0 margin-bottom-3\">The Ghosts of Five Supernovas</h1>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-row media-detail-hero__content-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-6\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"p-md margin-0 media-detail-hero__description\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<strong>Explanation:</strong> The ghosts of five supernovas haunt this extraordinary <a href=\"https://app.astrobin.com/i/jvnafq?r=D\" rel=\"noopener\">image</a>. It was acquired at <a href=\"https://www.planetary.org/space-images/morocco-oukameden-sky-survey\" rel=\"noopener\">Oukaïmeden Observatory</a> in <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/wet-and-dry-morocco-144677/\">Morocco</a> with approximately 200 hours of observations and shows a large patch of the sky, equivalent to the <a href=\"https://lco.global/spacebook/sky/using-angles-describe-positions-and-apparent-sizes-objects/\" rel=\"noopener\">area</a> of one thousand full moons tiled together, in the constellation of <a href=\"https://noirlab.edu/public/education/constellations/auriga/\" rel=\"noopener\">Auriga</a> (the <a href=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1706793987472-2e3b3ec44fcc\" rel=\"noopener\">Charioteer</a>). From left to right, the five supernova remnants visible across the field are <a href=\"https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2017/01/aa29848-16\" rel=\"noopener\">G181.1+9.5</a>, <a href=\"https://articles.adsabs.harvard.edu/pdf/1998A%26A...331..661K\" rel=\"noopener\">G182.4+4.3</a>, <a href=\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/link_gateway/2018MNRAS.478.1987H/PUB_HTML\" rel=\"noopener\">G179.0+2.6</a>, <a href=\"https://academic.oup.com/mnras/article/448/4/3196/955844\" rel=\"noopener\">G180.0−1.7</a> (Sh2-240, the <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap240227.html\" rel=\"noopener\">Spaghetti Nebula</a>), and <a href=\"https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full_html/2011/08/aa17179-11/aa17179-11.html\" rel=\"noopener\">G178.2−4.2</a>. They are highlighted in the <a href=\"image/2609/5SNR_Auriga_annotated_1000.jpg\">annotated image</a>, together with <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap250227.html\" rel=\"noopener\">open cluster</a> <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap100305.html\" rel=\"noopener\">M37</a> and the <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap260317.html\" rel=\"noopener\">Tadpole Nebula</a>. As each explosion <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap250108.html\" rel=\"noopener\">expanded into space</a>, it created a growing shell of shocked gas and delicate filamentary structures shown in red (<a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap050930.html\" rel=\"noopener\">hydrogen</a>) and blue (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doubly_ionized_oxygen\" rel=\"noopener\">oxygen</a>), respectively. These ancient stellar explosions happened independently; they are at various distances up to about several thousands of <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/exoplanets/what-is-a-light-year/\">light-years</a> away from Earth and have estimated ages up to <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/ap260107.html\" rel=\"noopener\">tens of thousands of years old</a>. Early humans may have seen them as bright new stars, fading over weeks or months.<br><br><strong>APOD&#8217;s email for image submissions has changed.</strong> Please see: <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/apod/lib/apsubmit2015.html\" rel=\"noopener\">APOD Submissions.</a><br><strong>APOD&#8217;s main NASA site is <a href=\"https://asterisk.apod.com/viewtopic.php?t=45023\" rel=\"noopener\">moving</a> </strong>: From <a href=\"https://apod.nasa.gov/\" rel=\"noopener\">apod.nasa.gov</a> to <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod\">science.nasa.gov/apod</a><br><strong>Tomorrow&#8217;s picture: </strong>what&#8217;s next?<br>\t\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"display-none desktop:display-block desktop:grid-col-1\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-5 margin-top-3 desktop:margin-top-0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<table class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-table width-full\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tbody>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Date</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSeptember 24, 2026\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Credit</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://app.astrobin.com/u/Sacrednight\" rel=\"noopener\">Stephane Vetter</a>, <a href=\"https://app.astrobin.com/u/yann_sainty\" rel=\"noopener\">Yann Sainty</a>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">Authors &amp; editors:</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tCecilia Chirenti, Robert Nemiroff, Jerry Bonnell, Keighley Rockcliffe\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<tr class=\"media-detail-hero__meta-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<th scope=\"row\" class=\"label padding-y-1\">A service of:</th>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<td class=\"p-sm padding-y-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://science.gsfc.nasa.gov/astrophysics/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ASD</a> at <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NASA</a> / <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/centers/goddard/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GSFC</a>,<br /><a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/learn/about-science-activation/\" target=\"_blank\">NASA Science Activation</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://www.mtu.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Michigan Tech. U.</a>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</tbody>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</table>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t</div>",
